EXPERIMENT 40 – API TESTING USING APACHE JMETER
AIM
To use Apache JMeter to create test cases for API testing and verify the status codes and the response data.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter and rename the Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group.
3. Set Number of Threads = 5, Ramp-up Period = 5 seconds and Loop Count = 1.
4. Add HTTP Request Defaults for the API server.
5. Test Case 1: GET /posts/1 with Response Assertion for status code 200 and JSON Assertion for $.id = 1.
6. Test Case 2: GET /posts/9999 with Response Assertion for status code 404. Select Ignore Status.
7. Test Case 3: GET /posts?userId=1 with JSON Assertion for $[0].userId = 1.
8. Add View Results Tree and Summary Report.
9. Run the plan and verify the status codes and response data.
INPUT – TEST PLAN CONFIGURATION
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Number of Threads	5
Thread Group	Ramp-up Period	5 seconds
Thread Group	Loop Count	1
HTTP Request Defaults	Protocol / Server	https / jsonplaceholder.typicode.com
TC1	Request	GET /posts/1
TC1	Response Assertion	Response Code = 200
TC1	JSON Assertion	$.id = 1
TC2	Request	GET /posts/9999
TC2	Response Assertion	Response Code = 404
TC2	Ignore Status	Selected
TC3	Request	GET /posts?userId=1
TC3	JSON Assertion	$[0].userId = 1

OUTPUT
Summary Report
Label	Samples	Error %
TC1: GET /posts/1	5	0.00%
TC2: GET /posts/9999	5	0.00%
TC3: GET /posts?userId=1	5	0.00%
TOTAL	15	0.00%

RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to create test cases for API testing and verify the status codes and response data.
